15326f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-online-censorship-grows-after-cockroach-protests/a-79976982?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since anti-government Cockroach protests erupted, journalists and creators say their content is increasingly being restricted on social media in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>ICJ to rule on Rohingya genocide case against Myanmar: What to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3dd01c946608cdaa64ed421138a7d8f84a9370bf45be51108d101626e753874</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:23:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T14:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434--76de3c2375bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icj-to-rule-on-rohingya-genocide-case-against-myanmar-what-to-know/a-79981434?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ICJ is set to decide whether Myanmar's military operations in Rakhine State a decade ago were carried out with the intent to destroy the country's Rohingya minority, in whole or in part.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Axes and cutlasses: Violence on Nigeria's election campaign trail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65db7b82279014f0ea6a1dce0722a5e94fea7529e9f1b9aa207b0f1d6b27675e</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:23:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/axes-and-cutlasses-violence-on-nigeria-s-election-campaign-trail/a-79978467--351fdc554734.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/axes-and-cutlasses-violence-on-nigeria-s-election-campaign-trail/a-79978467?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria's January 2027 elections approach, political violence and thuggery at campaign rallies and town hall meetings raise concerns about voter safety.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Latin America's mega-prisons: Can El Salvador's model work?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:419e4a95d81a88f229f58565e9ecfb99484413e825ceb61b4e855693e589475f</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:23:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T10:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/latin-america-s-mega-prisons-can-el-salvador-s-model-work/a-79973524--e4fa38fb46de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/latin-america-s-mega-prisons-can-el-salvador-s-model-work/a-79973524?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">El Salvador's mega-prison has become a model for governments across Latin America seeking to combat organized crime. But experts question whether the approach is effective, sustainable or compatible with human rights.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>APEC summit: Xi, Trump and Putin gather in Shenzhen, China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40b64cb8385e9d954352dbf274d80b53f21587be6cba7b1976769ce01cfe6ebb</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:23:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-xi-trump-and-putin-gather-in-shenzhen-china/live-79964719--666f7e6268c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/apec-summit-xi-trump-and-putin-gather-in-shenzhen-china/live-79964719?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The presidents of China, Russia and the US have greeted each other amid the APEC summit in Shenzhen. This comes a day ahead of the trilateral talks between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin and Donald Trump. Follow DW live.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How a green economy could help reverse climate change</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d3096184cdffdbfc17ce11f22c0b202430d2c55d6735cecdadef02716ad899f</id><updated>2026-11-18T17:23:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T09:02:00Z</published><link rel="a